Q-1 needs exactly one \\\"shall\\\"; REQ-4 needs exactly one \\\"shall\\\"; REQ-11 needs exactly one \\\"shall\\\"\",\n \"[lint L4 vague] NFR-1 uses a vague word (\\\"quickly\\\") with no number\",\n \"[lint L9 size] 17 requirements / 37 ACs is over the budget for a feature; split into a run sequence\",\n \"[lint L11 observable] AC-1.3's Then doesn't name something observable (response, row, call, screen); AC-1.6's Then doesn't name something observable (response, row, call, screen); AC-2.3's Then doesn't name something observable (response, row, call, screen)\",\n \"[critic critical] REQ-5 REQ-5 says the lowest bucket is always 7–30 whatever the threshold, but REQ-6 says it starts at the configured threshold; AC-5.1 and AC-6.1 use the same setup (threshold 5, invoice 6 days past due) and expect opposite results.\",\n \"[critic high] REQ-12 No requirement or AC covers an invoice ID that does not exist in the existing system, whether on the detail endpoint or on POST /api/invoices/{id}/reminders; the status-code list has no 404 for this.\",\n \"[critic high] REQ-1 The current-behaviour artifact records 'no repository: this is new build work' and has no claims, yet REQ-1, REQ-2 and REQ-7 rely on unverified details of the existing .NET 8 API/Postgres, such as the status values 'paid'/'cancelled', a single billing email field, customer name and the user ID claim in the token.\",\n \"[critic high] REQ-1 Overdue means any status 'neither paid nor cancelled', so existing invoices with other statuses (draft, void, written-off, disputed, credited) or with a null due date would be classified overdue or break the rule; no AC covers these existing-data cases.\"\n]\n</artifact>\n\n<untrusted_document id=\"request\" source=\"cli\">\n# Invoice reminders\n\nA small web app for a bakery wholesaler. Staff see which customer invoices are overdue and send a reminder by email.\n\n## Requirements\n\n- When an invoice is 7 days past its due date, the system shall mark it overdue and show it on the overdue list.\n- When staff press \"Send reminder\" on an overdue invoice, the system shall email the customer a reminder with the invoice number, amount and due date.\n- The system shall record each reminder sent, with who sent it and when, and show the history on the invoice.\n- If an email cannot be delivered, the system shall show the failure on the invoice and keep it on the overdue list.\n- Staff shall be able to filter the overdue list by customer and by days overdue.\n\n## Screens\n\n- Overdue list (table, filters, a \"Send reminder\" button per row)\n- Invoice detail (amount, due date, reminder history, delivery failures)\n\n## Out of scope\n\nPayments, customer logins, SMS reminders.\n\n## Stack\n\nClient's existing .NET 8 API with a React front end. Postgres.\n</untrusted_document>\n\nRepair this spec so every finding is fixed. Keep requirement IDs stable where the meaning doesn't change. Change nothing the findings don't need."}